course: dictionary
lesson: 4800
title: When someone is made to feel small
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To humiliate someone is to make them feel very ashamed, foolish or small, especially in front of other people. Humiliate is a verb, so it changes: humiliates, humiliated, humiliating. Look at the clues in this sentence: «A prank is cruel when only one person is hurt or humiliated and the others laugh; that is bullying.» The words cruel, hurt and the others laugh show that humiliated is something bad that happens to a person.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. "A prank is cruel when only one person is made to feel foolish and the others laugh." It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Stories show the feeling inside the body. «Being humiliated in front of others burns in a special way: your face goes hot, you want the ground to swallow you.» The writer does not say "humiliated" means shame, but the hot face and the wish to disappear show it. A humiliating moment is one that leaves you feeling small.
fact: Humiliate is a verb: humiliates, humiliated, humiliating.
fact: «Humiliate» means to make someone feel very ashamed, foolish or small, especially in front of other people.
fact: «Humiliating» describes something that makes a person feel this way, such as a humiliating defeat.
fact: Being laughed at by many people online can be very humiliating, so do not film pranks without agreement.
fact: You can notice the feeling in a story by looking at what the character's body does, such as a face going hot.
exercise: «A prank is cruel when only one person is hurt or humiliated and the others laugh.» What does humiliated mean here? | Very happy and proud | Given a prize for winning | *Made to feel very ashamed and small | Tired after running
exercise: «Being humiliated in front of others burns in a special way: your face goes hot.» What does a face going hot show? | Being very cold | *Shame and embarrassment | Someone is feeling calm | The sun is shining
exercise: Which word is the past tense of humiliate? | *humiliated | humiliating | humble | humiliates
test: «Will they be humiliated?» What does this question ask? | *Will they be made to feel small and ashamed? | Will they be given a medal? | Will they be late for school?
test: Which situation is most likely to humiliate someone? | Helping a friend with homework | *Being laughed at by a crowd for a silly mistake they made | Sharing a snack at lunch
exam: Which sentence shows a humiliating experience? | Going to the park with your gran | Getting a new bike for your birthday | *Losing a match 10-0 in front of the whole school and hearing everyone laugh
